{"version":1,"ops":[{"type":1,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1578560914,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDU6SXNzdWU1NDczNDM0OTc=","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/3994","origin":"github"},"title":"Support `datalad -f '{relpath}'`","message":"It would be convenient to be able get relative paths from the cmdline results for programatic post-processing. I.e. like this:\n\n```\n% datalad diff -f incoming^ -t incoming                 \n    added: 1008788_20227_2_0.zip (file)\n    added: 1008788_20249_2_0.zip (file)\n    added: 1008788_20252_2_0.zip (file)\n```\n\nbut just the relative path. Absolute is working already, relative not:\n\n```\n% datalad -f '{path}' diff -f incoming^ -t incoming                                                                                      \n/data/project/rehab_biobank/datalad_trial/1008788/.datalad/.gitattributes\n/data/project/rehab_biobank/datalad_trial/1008788/.datalad/config\n/data/project/rehab_biobank/datalad_trial/1008788/.gitattributes\n/data/project/rehab_biobank/datalad_trial/1008788/1008788_20227_2_0.zip\n/data/project/rehab_biobank/datalad_trial/1008788/1008788_20249_2_0.zip\n/data/project/rehab_biobank/datalad_trial/1008788/1008788_20252_2_0.zip\n\n% datalad -f '{relpath}' diff -f incoming^ -t incoming\nN/A\nN/A\nN/A\nN/A\nN/A\nN/A\n```","files":null}]}